		heading: 'What faith means in the Bible',
		bodyHtml: `<p>Faith is <strong>trust that leans its weight on someone</strong>. In the Bible its object is always our Father and what He has said. Hebrews defines it by its direction: &ldquo;Now faith is the assurance of things hoped for, the conviction of things not seen&rdquo; (Hebrews 11:1). Faith treats our Father&rsquo;s promise as solid ground, even while the promise is still on its way.</p><p>It is also how we are saved: &ldquo;For by grace you have been saved through faith&mdash;not your own doing; it is the gift of our Father&rdquo; (Ephesians 2:8). Faith does not earn the gift; it receives it.</p>`,
